 "summary": "The Lean theorem says the following. Take a wave amplitude `a` in the wave class W_α, with weight √ζ·P. Assume the phase normal of the field (V_r, V_θ, V_z, Φ) has polynomial jet bounds and satisfies 0 < b ≤ |n_Φ| ≤ M on the strip domain. Assume V_r ∈ M_{-κ}, V_θ ∈ M_0, V_z ∈ M_1 and 1/R ∈ M_0 (all unweighted), and 1/K_n = O(ε_n^{1/2}·slow^p). Then the curl remainder of the curl-generated coefficient lies in W_{α+1/2-κ}. The quoted paper Lemma 9.2 is a different result, so the declaration appears mispaired with the excerpt. The paper lemma concerns mean–wave and wave–wave transport products (w·∇*)v + (v·∇*)w, with exponent α+μ−1/2. The Lean result is about a curl remainder with exponent α+1/2−κ. The key caveat is that the core objects (`curlRemainder`, `coefficient`, `phaseNormal`, `MemClass`, `StripData`) are not visible, so faithfulness even to the candidate-manuscript lemma cannot be checked here.",
